# Third Eye World Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Ship Third Eye World to production readiness — a single Next.js app with a public marketing site (`/`) and an auth-gated mission platform, Third Eye Commons (`/app/*`), self-hostable via Docker.

**Architecture:** One Next.js 15 App-Router app, RSC-first with small client islands. Route groups `(marketing)` and `app/` give the two surfaces distinct layouts and an auth boundary while sharing one design system and one Docker image. Data in PostgreSQL via Prisma; auth via Auth.js (Credentials + JWT sessions, role in token). Animation via Motion + GSAP. Accessibility is a hard, CI-enforced requirement.

**Tech Stack:** Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS 4, Shadcn/ui, Motion (`motion/react`), GSAP + ScrollTrigger, Auth.js v5 (`next-auth@beta`), Prisma, PostgreSQL, argon2, Vitest + Testing Library, Playwright + `@axe-core/playwright`, ESLint + Prettier, Docker + docker-compose.

## Global Constraints

- Grounded content only — all copy/imagery sourced from `docs/instructions/` + the Third Eye Kit v2 dossier; **no invented product claims**.
- Accessibility floor: **WCAG 2.2 AA**, screen-reader-native, keyboard-first; `@axe-core/playwright` must report **zero serious/critical** violations on tested routes (CI gate).
- Performance: RSC by default; `'use client'` only on interactive leaves; animate **transform/opacity only**, never layout props; main JS bundle **< 200KB gzipped** target; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Anti-slop: UI built via the **`design-taste-frontend`** skill; **`design-review`** pass before each PR; one genuinely distinctive interactive element (haptic demo).
- Animation split: GSAP in its own webpack chunk, plugins lazy-loaded.
- Images via `next/image` only, never `<img>`.
- Auth reality: Credentials provider ⇒ **JWT session strategy** (not DB sessions); user `id` + `role` carried in the JWT and exposed on `session.user`.
- Git workflow: branches `main`/`prod`/`dev`; feature branches off `dev`; **every PR opened by Said (`sadeqisaidmohaddes-star`)** targeting `dev`; CI green required; **agent never merges — the user reviews and merges.** Feature commits authored by Said.
- Conventional Commits. Commit trailers per session settings.

