## Slice 2 — Data + Auth (branch `feature/data-auth` → PR by Said → `dev`)

**Deliverable:** Prisma schema + migration + seed; Auth.js Credentials signup/login with role; session exposes `id`+`role`; app shell at `/app` redirects unauthenticated users to `/app/login`. Tested with Postgres.

**Files:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts`, `src/lib/db.ts`, `src/lib/auth.ts`, `src/lib/auth-password.ts`, `src/lib/validation.ts`, `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`, `src/app/app/layout.tsx`, `src/app/app/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/app/signup/page.tsx`, `src/app/app/(authed)/layout.tsx`, `src/actions/auth.ts`, `tests/unit/auth-password.test.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, `types/next-auth.d.ts`.

**Interfaces produced:**
- `auth()` — server session getter (from Auth.js) returning `{ user: { id: string, role: Role, email: string } } | null`.
- `hashPassword(pw: string): Promise<string>`, `verifyPassword(pw, hash): Promise<boolean>`.
- `signUp(input): Promise<{ok:true}|{ok:false,error:string}>` server action.
- Prisma models per spec §7.

- [ ] **Prisma schema** `prisma/schema.prisma`:

```prisma
generator client { provider = "prisma-client-js" }
datasource db { provider = "postgresql"; url = env("DATABASE_URL") }

enum Role { BLIND_TRAVELER FAMILY CLINICIAN ENGINEER SUPPORTER }
enum WaitStatus { PENDING CONTACTED ENROLLED }

model User {
  id           String  @id @default(cuid())
  email        String  @unique
  passwordHash String
  role         Role
  emailVerifiedAt DateTime?
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
  profile      Profile?
  reactions    Reaction[]
  waitlist     WaitlistEntry?
  contributor  ContributorInterest?
  updates      Update[]
}
model Profile {
  userId      String @id
  user        User   @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  displayName String
  bio         String?
  region      String?
  a11yPrefs   Json   @default("{\"reducedMotion\":false,\"highContrast\":false,\"textScale\":1}")
}
model Update {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  authorId    String?
  author      User?    @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id])
  title       String
  body        String
  publishedAt DateTime @default(now())
  reactions   Reaction[]
}
model Reaction {
  id       String @id @default(cuid())
  updateId String
  update   Update @relation(fields: [updateId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  userId   String
  user     User   @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  kind     String
  @@unique([updateId, userId])
}
model WaitlistEntry {
  id            String     @id @default(cuid())
  userId        String     @unique
  user          User       @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  role          Role
  region        String?
  deviceContext String?
  status        WaitStatus @default(PENDING)
  createdAt     DateTime   @default(now())
}
model ContributorInterest {
  id         String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId     String   @unique
  user       User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  githubUrl  String?
  focusAreas String[]
  note       String?
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())
}
```
  (No Auth.js adapter session tables needed — JWT sessions. Keep it minimal.)

- [ ] **Migrate:** `npx prisma migrate dev --name init` against a local/dev Postgres (docker `postgres:16` for sandbox). Generate client.
- [ ] **`src/lib/db.ts`:** singleton PrismaClient (guard against dev hot-reload).
- [ ] **Password util** `src/lib/auth-password.ts` using argon2. **TDD:** `tests/unit/auth-password.test.ts` — hash≠plain, verify(pw,hash)=true, verify(wrong,hash)=false → fail → implement → pass.
